gs so they only fire after the visitor has explicitly accepted. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=text%20~%20%22project%20%3D%20SFCC%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20AAB-003\\*%22%20or%20summary%20~%20%22project%20%3D%20SFCC%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20AAB-003\\*%22%20or%20key%20%3D%20%22project%20%3D%20SFCC%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20AAB-003%22%20ORDER%20BY%20created%20DESC](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=text%20~%20%22project%20%3D%20SFCC%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20AAB-003*%22%20or%20summary%20~%20%22project%20%3D%20SFCC%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20AAB-003*%22%20or%20key%20%3D%20%22project%20%3D%20SFCC%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20AAB-003%22%20ORDER%20BY%20created%20DESC) |\n| AAB-004 | A-B Testing | The system will ensure the data layer populated in AAB-002 includes the attributes required for Optimizely audience segmentation - such as authenticated state, customer group, loyalty status, storefront region, new vs returning visitor and device type. | Zimmermann | ALL |  | Confirmed | Confirmed by Tell No Lies that Optimizely and Crazy Egg are out of the GTM container. They need separate frontend tags. The requirement should be \"The PWA Kit will load the Optimizely script directly on the page head, so that it initialises before render and A/B test variates can be applied without flicker.\" For Optimizely specifically, it is one snippet for all environments and it is only on the US website. | [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=text%20~%20%22project%20%3D%20SFCC%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20AAB-004\\*%22%20or%20summary%20~%20%22project%20%3D%20SFCC%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20AAB-004\\*%22%20or%20key%20%3D%20%22project%20%3D%20SFCC%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20AAB-004%22%20ORDER%20BY%20created%20DESC](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=text%20~%20%22project%20%3D%20SFCC%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20AAB-004*%22%20or%20summary%20~%20%22project%20%3D%20SFCC%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20AAB-004*%22%20or%20key%20%3D%20%22project%20%3D%20SFCC%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20AAB-004%22%20ORDER%20BY%20created%20DESC) |\n| AAB-005 | Heatmapping & Session Replay | The system will ensure the data layer populated in AAB-002 includes page type, authenticated state and storefront region to support Crazy Egg segmentation and suppression configuration. | Zimmermann | ALL |  | Confirmed | Confirmed by Tell No Lies that Optimizely and Crazy Egg are out of the GTM container. They need separate frontend tags. The requirement should be \"The PWA Kit will load the Crazy Egg script directly on the page head, to enable full session recording and heatmap capture from page load.\" | [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=text%20~%20%22project%20%3D%20SFCC%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20AAB-005\\*%22%20or%20summary%20~%20%22project%20%3D%20SFCC%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20AAB-005\\*%22%20or%20key%20%3D%20%22project%20%3D%20SFCC%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20AAB-005%22%20ORDER%20BY%20created%20DESC](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=text%20~%20%22project%20%3D%20SFCC%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20AAB-005*%22%20or%20summary%20~%20%22project%20%3D%20SFCC%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20AAB-005*%22%20or%20key%20%3D%20%22project%20%3D%20SFCC%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20AAB-005%22%20ORDER%20BY%20created%20DESC) |"
